<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The script is completely deterministic with zero stochastic dependencies, regenerates bressloff_v1_metrics.csv byte-for-byte identically on CLI execution, and provides a fast (~1.5 s) --self-test mode that verifies all four fixture SHA-256 digests, calibration parity, map inversion, magnification error bounds, and spectral classifications. It automatically selects the headless Agg backend when --no-show, --self-test, or no DISPLAY is present, and both requirements.txt and requirements.lock.txt pin a working Python environment. Deduct 4 points because the script docstring does not document its CLI flags (--out, --csv, --gif, --no-show, --self-test) or example invocations, README.md mentions only --gif PATH, and AGENTS.md omits the script from its top-level command list. Deduct 2 points because run_bressloff_analysis and make_gif write to output_png, output_csv, and output_gif without creating parent directories via parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True), raising FileNotFoundError if a non-existent output directory is passed. Deduct 2 points for minor precision-bound drift between README.md ('<= 6.7e-16'), the script docstring ('~1e-15'), and actual self-test output ('2.22e-16'). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1–L80: Module docstring lacking CLI usage examples, followed by automatic headless Agg backend selection. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1-L80>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1628–L1739: Comprehensive deterministic self_test() suite and argparse CLI entrypoint in main(). <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1628-L1739>; requirements.lock.txt L1–L51: Pinned dependency lockfile for the ./venv execution environment. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L51>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Source and data traceability: 94/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "All five primary papers (Bressloff et al. 2001, Bressloff et al. 2002, Ermentrout and Cowan 1979, Rule et al. 2011, and Horton and Hoyt 1991) are cited with resolvable DOIs and PMIDs in the script docstring, datasets/bressloff/README.md, and datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib. The upstream repository MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants is pinned to exact commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c with full MIT license attribution to Karacsony and Holzapfel, and horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json is clearly distinguished as a repository-authored empirical fixture. Runtime SHA-256 verification via verify_fixture_checksums guards all four JSON files in datasets/bressloff/. Deduct 4 points because driven-neural-fields-registry.json is SHA-256-pinned and described in datasets/bressloff/README.md as providing the Gaussian negative control (mackay_gaussian_kernel_negative_check from Tamekue, Prandi and Chitour 2024), yet the script never reads that file beyond checksum verification and Tamekue et al. (2024) is absent from paper_citations.bib. Deduct 2 points because Klüver (1966), the foundational source for the four form-constant taxonomy named throughout the script, lacks a formal bibliographic entry. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L11–L37: Primary literature DOIs/PMIDs and upstream MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit hash in module docstring. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L11-L37>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L87–L93: SHA-256 checksum dictionary pinning all four JSON fixtures, including the otherwise unread driven-neural-fields-registry.json. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L87-L93>; datasets/bressloff/README.md L7–L39: Provenance table, fixture caveats, primary literature links, and MIT license notice. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/datasets/bressloff/README.md#L7-L39>; datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib L1–L69: BibTeX entries for the five primary papers with DOIs and PMIDs. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib#L1-L69>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphological realism / specimen match: 72/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "On the flat cortical sheet, the four gallery panels clearly distinguish vertical rolls, oblique rolls, square lattices, and hexagonal lattices, and the Tunnel/Rings retinal pullback produces concentric rings that dilate with eccentricity as expected for Klüver's tunnel form constant. Panel D also provides a clean visual comparison between the Bressloff map's linear magnification and the empirical human V1 curve of Horton and Hoyt (1991). Deduct 10 points because the Spiral/Funnel retinal pullback (Col 2, fig33_rhombic_even_roll) fails to produce a logarithmic spiral or radial funnel, instead rendering bilaterally symmetric heart/chevron loops with vertical-meridian cusps caused by arctan2(vg, abs(ug)). Deduct 8 points because _eval_xy renders scalar tanh(sharpness * max_phi |val|) in continuous twilight_shifted pseudocolor (and make_gif forces noncontoured mode) rather than Bressloff's oriented contour segments, causing the Cobweb and Honeycomb retinal pullbacks at 160x160 resolution to appear as radially warped moiré spot interference. Deduct 6 points because no empirical subject drawings or digitized paper curves are overlaid, and Panel C plots all 20 Floquet boundary curves across five forcing amplitudes (0.4 to 1.2) on top of one another under two legend labels while failing upstream acceptance (RMS beta error 0.154 > 0.10). Deduct 4 points because planform_modes assigns p_scale = 0.35 to the second cobweb mode, creating a discontinuous phase jump at the loop boundary in docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif. Evidence: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): Composite 4x4 figure showing distinct cortical lattices, concentric tunnel pullback, cusped heart-shaped spiral pullback, warped moire cobweb/honeycomb pullbacks, and multi-amplitude Floquet overlay. — bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 9b18c52, image/png, 1048700 B, 2029×2087 px, artifact_sha256 b1c581d309d1ca62f759f511d26db59cb769c50d4aa1615f14631ebca9a943d4 (sha256 b1c581d309d1ca62f759f511d26db59cb769c50d4aa1615f14631ebca9a943d4), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif (generated output, not in repo): 36-frame phase-drift animation forced to noncontoured mode with visible cobweb phase discontinuity and bilateral cusp in the spiral panel. — docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 9b18c52, image/gif, 2282654 B, 640×340 px, 36 frames, artifact_sha256 12087533329905e1581829715b978712ba3293d1dc6daea2b2e6d70615b13b11 (sha256 12087533329905e1581829715b978712ba3293d1dc6daea2b2e6d70615b13b11), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L838–L865: Scalar max_phi envelope rendering and arctan2(vg, abs(ug)) hemifield reflection producing the vertical-meridian cusp. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L838-L865>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1404–L1436: Panel C loop plotting all 20 boundary_curves across five forcing amplitudes from rule-2011-floquet.json under two legend entries. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1404-L1436>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

